      "label": "Text",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sitting bored on my bed one dusk,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "half the beaded curtain peeled back."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In no mood to awaken yet no mood to sleep,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "clothes half-worn and eyes half-slack."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A sudden gust of wind pushes forth the boat,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "in dreams a war with the borisin we wage."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Knife in hand, black and red horses leap on,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Alongside my husband's warship, in fight I engage."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Two twittering orioles land on their branch,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "with karma past doth this life's grief cast."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ten times reborn, with all its love and hate,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "how hard can one take of a husband lost."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Gazing up I now see daylight through that verdigris,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "those past loves and past lives seen only in reveries."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-72126a1537df2867"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When the dragon turns red, then the green pines shall shed."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Cast by the wind of a cold morning,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Feeling the weight of your suffering."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-10117febdbe2a80d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When the dragon turns red, then the green pines shall shed."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Spinning our glory through time and space,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When will I next come to see your face?"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-122cc1b32fed1705"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When the dragon turns red, then the green pines shall shed."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Wantonly drinking the silver moon,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "How many times must we be entombed?"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-477091edb79546cc"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When the dragon turns red, then the green pines shall shed."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Pass like a dream out of sight and mind,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "six hundred years in this mortal bind."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-39f78e544fde0238"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
